    "b-25-quick-start-solution-steering-is-opt-26": {
      "id": "b-25-quick-start-solution-steering-is-opt-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Solution steering is optional and goes last. Leave it out and the run chooses its own approach. If you hold a constraint, such as \"reuse this helper\" or \"no new dependency\", say it, because the run can't honor a preference you didn't state."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-25-quick-start-a-brief-worth-running-27": {
      "id": "b-25-quick-start-a-brief-worth-running-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A brief worth running:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-25-quick-start-bash-28": {
      "id": "b-25-quick-start-bash-28",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "bash"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "archon workflow run archon-ship --branch fix/upload-timeout \"$(cat <<'BRIEF'\nProblem: uploads over ~8 MB fail with a 504 after 30s. The proxy read timeout is\n30s and the upload handler streams to disk before responding.\n\nWhy it matters: this is the top support complaint this month.\n\nWhy now: the export feature ships next week and its files are 20-50 MB.\n\nOutcome: a 50 MB upload completes, and a stuck upload still fails instead of hanging.\n\nInvariants: no change to the storage layout or the public upload API; memory use\nmust not scale with file size.\n\nAcceptance: a 50 MB upload succeeds end to end; a test covers the timeout path.\n\nSteering: prefer streaming straight to storage over raising the timeout.\nBRIEF\n)\" --detach"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-25-quick-start-archon-ship-takes-an-i-29": {
      "id": "b-25-quick-start-archon-ship-takes-an-i-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "archon-ship",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " takes an issue or request to a reviewed pull request. It reaches GitHub through the forge plugin, so run "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon plugin add coleam00/Archon/plugins/forge-github",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " first; your "
        },
        {
          "insert": "gh auth login",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "GH_TOKEN",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") is the credential it uses. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--detach",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " starts the run in the background and returns at once."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
